": -5.12, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": -5.95, "poll_sd": 10.89, "poll_weight": 0.18, "fundamentals": {"margin": -1.3, "lean": -7.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": -2.0, "money": -0.5}, "rating_margin": -7.67, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.26, "baseline_margin": -5.27, "analyst_adjustment": 0.77, "key_factors": ["R+7 district lean with incumbent Crane running for a second term", "Polls show a closer race than the district lean, including a Democratic-sponsored poll at Crane +2", "Crane holds a large fundraising and cash-on-hand edge with $2.1M in fall ads reserved", "Raters split between Likely R and Lean R; markets price Crane around 65%"], "rationale": "The district's R+7 lean and Crane's incumbency and money advantage point to a Republican favorite, but recent polling shows Nez within a few points and markets price this closer to a tossup than a Likely R race. A modest tilt toward the Democrat from the fundamentals baseline is justified by the polling and market evidence.", "watch": "Any additional independent polling or a shift in the national House environment could move this between Lean R and Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Eli Crane (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Eli Crane seeks a second term in a northeastern Arizona district that leans Republican by about seven points, facing a rematch against former Navajo Nation President Jonathan Nez. Crane has raised roughly $9.5 million and holds a cash advantage, with $2.1 million reserved for fall advertising, while Nez has raised about $3.5 million and focused his campaign on water, housing, and cost-of-living issues. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot.\n\nMost race raters call the contest Likely Republican, though a few rate it Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Crane roughly a two-thirds chance. Available polling from August shows a single-digit race, with one survey putting Crane up just two points. The forecast expects Crane to win by a modest margin, with meaningful uncertainty given thin and partly partisan-sponsored polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1703, "margin": -5.61}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2296, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2721, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1924, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2064, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2601, "margin": -4.5}]}